   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Share of people aged 15 and above that made or received a digital payment</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2017-12-29" value="37.33" year="2017"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-12-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-30"></period-end>
     <target value="0.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Alternative indicators were used to analyze the efficacy of the prior action. Findex collects equivalent data to RI7, namely, the share of people aged 15 and above that made or received a digital payment, which increased from 37.33 percent in 2017 to 52.11 percent in 2021 (the only close data points available), representing a 140 percent increase (14.8 percentage points). Considering the rising digitalization trends, particularly after the COVID pandemic, it would be expected for this share to have continued increasing in 2022 and onwards.&amp;nbsp; Likewise, according to household survey data (EMTIC Hogares), the percentage of people over 18 years ofge who made purchases through the Internet increased from 21.6 percent in 2020 to 24.9 percent in 2021 (the latest data point available)&lt;/p&amp;gt;

&lt;p&amp;gt;Evidence: Findex Database 2021&amp;nbsp;https://www.worldbank.org/en/publication/globalfindex&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="51.11"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
